== chat <chat:3> "💬 e2ehost - New message in after-recreate"
   type: meeting; members: owner
-- <msg:1> helper (html)
   | <!-- codex-helper-outbox:<marker> --><p><strong>🔧 Helper:</strong></p>
   | <p>Work chat created: s001.<br>
   | Working directory: <root>/work/after-recreate</p>
-- <msg:2> helper (html)
   | <!-- codex-helper-outbox:<marker> --><p><strong>🔧 Helper:</strong></p>
   | <p>💬 Work chat is ready.<br>
   | Send a task in this chat. Codex will start automatically and continue this session.<br>
   | Status: waiting for your first task.<br>
   | Session: s001<br>
   | Project: after-recreate<br>
   | Working directory: <root>/work/after-recreate<br>
   | Commands: <code>helper status</code> or <code>!status</code>, <code>helper stats</code>, <code>helper help</code>, <code>helper close</code> to close this Codex session in Teams.<br>
   | Need more details? Send <code>helper status</code>.</p>

== cli
$ cxp teams control --recreate
   exit 1
   stderr| Error: recreating the control chat creates a new Teams chat and sends messages; rerun with --yes
$ cxp teams control --recreate --yes
   exit 0
   stdout| Waiting for the running Teams helper...
   stdout| Teams control chat recreated: https://teams.microsoft.com/l/chat/<chat:2>/0?tenantId=e2e00000-0000-4000-8000-00000000te57
   stdout| Title: 🏠 Codex Control - e2ehost
   stdout| Chat ID: <chat:2>
   stdout| Previous Chat ID: <chat:1>
   stdout| The running Teams helper now uses the new control chat.
